📊 MANOVA (Multivariate Analysis of Variance)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

What is MANOVA?

**MANOVA** is an extension of ANOVA used when there are **multiple dependent variables**.

It tests whether group means differ across **a combination of dependent variables**.

---

Why MANOVA is Needed?

* Handles multiple outcomes simultaneously
* Controls Type-I error
* Captures relationships between dependent variables

---

ANOVA vs MANOVA

| Feature             | ANOVA                  | MANOVA     |
| ------------------- | ---------------------- | ---------- |
| Dependent variables | One                    | Multiple   |
| Error rate          | Higher with many tests | Controlled |
| Relationships       | Ignored                | Considered |

---

Hypotheses in MANOVA

* **H₀**: Group means are equal across all dependent variables
* **H₁**: At least one group differs

---

Assumptions of MANOVA

* Multivariate normality
* Homogeneity of covariance matrices
* Independence of observations
* No multicollinearity

---

Test Statistics in MANOVA

* Wilks’ Lambda
* Pillai’s Trace
* Hotelling’s Trace
* Roy’s Largest Root

(Used to decide statistical significance)

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

When to Use MANOVA?

* Multiple related outcome variables
* Experimental studies
* Behavioral, medical, and social science research
* Multivariate business metrics

---

⚠️ Limitations of MANOVA

* Sensitive to assumption violations
* Complex interpretation
* Requires larger sample sizes

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Concept Comparison Summary

| Concept             | Purpose                   | Output               |
| ------------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------- |
| Confidence Interval | Estimate population range | Interval             |
| A/B Testing         | Compare two variants      | Decision             |
| MANOVA              | Compare multiple outcomes | Overall significance |

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚠️ Important Notes

* CI provides estimation, not decisions
* A/B testing focuses on practical impact
* MANOVA reduces multiple testing errors
* Always validate assumptions before tests

